cellGcmSys: the SET_REFERENCE fence queue publishes a slot only after its fence is stored in it (release/acquire).

Cause: gcm_ref_push_at stored the queue slot with a plain store and then the volatile tail; MinGW gcc -O2 emits the tail
store first (objdump of cellGcmSys.c.obj: `mov %r9d,s_ref_qtail` before `mov %ebx,(%rax,%rdx,4)`). The poll path
(cellGcm_ref_on_poll, a guest thread spinning on ctrl->ref) publishes under its own lock, so between the two stores it
could see the new tail, write the slot's stale word into ctrl->ref (0 while fewer than GCM_REF_QLEN fences were ever
queued) and move head past the fence that landed a moment later. An equality waiter then never sees its value again.
Ratchet & Clank 1 (Collection) waits for ref == its last frame fence each frame (func_00523A48 / func_0052A59C /
func_0052A780, 40 000 x usleep(50) then "Renderer timed out", and keeps waiting): run rc1-stall2 drained fence 0x7B1
(GCM_REFLOG), the main thread waited for 0x7B1 (r28) and ctrl->ref read 0x00000000 at 105/120/140 s, get == put; the
game stopped presenting at t=84 s; rc1-boot1 stopped the same way at 92.8 s. Intermittent (rc1-stall1 ran past it).
Fix: __atomic_store_n(tail, RELEASE) after the slot, __atomic_load_n(tail, ACQUIRE) before reading it. Not changed: the
overflow branch (producer bumps head without the publication lock; needs 4096 queued fences, never seen here).
Upstream candidate (general runtime race, any title with fence waits). R&C port patch 7042.

--- a/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
+++ b/libs/video/cellGcmSys.c
@@ -2076,7 +2076,16 @@
         if (PS3_LOG_FIRST(_o, 4)) fprintf(stderr, "[cellGcmSys] fence queue overflow -- oldest dropped\n");
     }
     s_ref_q[t % GCM_REF_QLEN] = v;
-    s_ref_qtail = t + 1;
+    /* R&C patch 7042: publish the slot before the tail. A plain store let the
+     * compiler (MinGW gcc -O2) store the new tail first and the slot second;
+     * a guest thread polling ctrl->ref (cellGcm_ref_on_poll) in between read
+     * the slot before the fence landed in it, wrote that stale word (0 while
+     * fewer than GCM_REF_QLEN fences were ever queued) into ctrl->ref and
+     * moved head past the real fence. The equality-waiter then waited for a
+     * value the register never shows again (R&C 1 Collection: "Renderer
+     * timed out" with ref = 0 after fence 0x7B1 was drained). Release here
+     * pairs with the acquire in gcm_ref_publish_one. */
+    __atomic_store_n(&s_ref_qtail, t + 1, __ATOMIC_RELEASE);
 }

